# Issue 1 — Toggle Task Status uses an unset variable
## Feature: Task Tracker — toggling a task between outstanding/completed (section 1.1)

## (1.1) Original pseudocode:
WHEN user clicks a task's circle/checkbox
    Get the clicked task's ID
    CALL toggleTaskStatus(taskId, isCompleted)
END

FUNCTION toggleTaskStatus(taskId, isCompleted)
    DECLARE let newStatus = isCompleted === false
    Update task in Firebase using taskId, set completed = newStatus
    RETURN newStatus
END FUNCTION

## (1.2) Trace table — before fix:
Test:               |Click checkbox on an outstanding task	                                
Input:              |taskId = "t1", isCompleted = (never retrieved — not declared anywhere before the 
                    |CALL)	                                                                                
Expected result:	|newStatus becomes true (task flips to completed)    
Actual result:      |isCompleted is undefined, so newStatus = (undefined === false) → false, every time, regardless of the task's real state
			
## (1.3) Corrected pseudocode:
WHEN user clicks a task's circle/checkbox
    Get the clicked task's ID
    Get the clicked task's current completed value
    STORE it as isCompleted
    CALL toggleTaskStatus(taskId, isCompleted)
END

## (1.4) Trace table — after fix (retest):
Test	                                |Input	                            |Expected result 	|Actual result
Click checkbox on an outstanding task	|isCompleted = false (now retrieved)|newStatus = true	|(false === false) → true — pass
Click checkbox on a completed task	    |isCompleted = true (now retrieved)	|newStatus = false	|(true === false) → false — pass

